1
00:00:11,230 --> 00:00:14,460
(Ryu Seil)

2
00:00:18,880 --> 00:00:22,340
(Ha Junghoon)

3
00:00:26,410 --> 00:00:29,660
(Lee Jungchan)

4
00:00:33,480 --> 00:00:36,980
(Jeong Siwan)

5
00:00:42,340 --> 00:00:47,020
(Boy, with Caution)

6
00:00:53,900 --> 00:00:55,930
Okay, that's about all I want to ask.

7
00:00:57,950 --> 00:01:00,030
You said you can
start working tomorrow, right?

8
00:01:00,030 --> 00:01:00,980
Yes.

9
00:01:04,319 --> 00:01:04,340
(Experience: Seojin High School, contract teacher; Nakwon High School, contract teacher;
Saebit High School, contract teacher; Cheongga High School, contract teacher)

10
00:01:04,340 --> 00:01:06,750
You should have other schools
to choose from.
(Experience: Seojin High School, contract teacher; Nakwon High School, contract teacher;
Saebit High School, contract teacher; Cheongga High School, contract teacher)

11
00:01:06,750 --> 00:01:09,300
Why did you come back to us?

12
00:01:17,190 --> 00:01:18,240
Here's the final question:

13
00:01:18,240 --> 00:01:23,510
in your opinion, would you think
you're what you'd think is a good teacher?

14
00:01:31,910 --> 00:01:34,229
I used to think so.

15
00:02:10,750 --> 00:02:12,390
This is the staff restroom.

16
00:02:13,770 --> 00:02:15,030
Are you a teacher?

17
00:02:17,820 --> 00:02:19,050
Not yet.

18
00:02:20,820 --> 00:02:22,280
You're a senior, right?

19
00:02:27,690 --> 00:02:30,150
Did you mistake this
for the nurse's office?

20
00:02:30,690 --> 00:02:31,800
I didn't.

21
00:02:33,710 --> 00:02:34,870
I know.

22
00:02:36,470 --> 00:02:38,730
But you'd better go
and get that checked.

23
00:02:41,920 --> 00:02:42,940
See you around.

24
00:03:10,820 --> 00:03:13,860
(Lee Hyunjae)

25
00:03:13,860 --> 00:03:26,790
(Boy, with Caution)
(Episode 1)

26
00:03:47,020 --> 00:03:49,510
(Mom)

27
00:03:56,750 --> 00:04:01,140
(When you want to be honest,
come to Random Chat and chat freely!)

28
00:04:10,160 --> 00:04:11,240
Son, you're back.

29
00:04:24,780 --> 00:04:27,530
What are you so busy with?
I can't even reach you.

30
00:04:27,810 --> 00:04:30,740
-Why didn't you answer the phone?
-Jiyoung and I ate first after waiting for you.

31
00:04:30,740 --> 00:04:33,130
-When did you arrive?
-30 minutes ago.

32
00:04:45,740 --> 00:04:46,540
Did you drink?

33
00:04:46,610 --> 00:04:48,610
Yes, I drank a little because of you.

34
00:04:52,500 --> 00:04:56,500
No matter what, you have to remember
to celebrate your wife's birthday.

35
00:04:56,760 --> 00:05:01,480
Oh, seeing you in a suit,
I thought you'd bring flowers back.

36
00:05:01,760 --> 00:05:02,960
I had an interview.

37
00:05:04,770 --> 00:05:05,670
I forgot.

38
00:05:05,870 --> 00:05:06,780
Sorry.

39
00:05:07,970 --> 00:05:09,080
What interview?

40
00:05:09,810 --> 00:05:11,470
Another contract job, right?

41
00:05:12,680 --> 00:05:16,280
How long do you plan
to do contract jobs?

42
00:05:16,280 --> 00:05:18,480
It makes it seem like you have some flaw.

43
00:05:19,680 --> 00:05:21,480
Son, she just didn't say it out loud.

44
00:05:21,480 --> 00:05:23,800
Jiyoung must be so worried about you.

45
00:05:24,710 --> 00:05:26,060
My income is not bad anyway.

46
00:05:26,060 --> 00:05:27,080
It's fine.

47
00:05:27,900 --> 00:05:30,510
Mom, well...

48
00:05:32,550 --> 00:05:34,200
If I don't answer the phone in the future,
don't come.

49
00:05:34,200 --> 00:05:35,630
-We...
-Mom.

50
00:05:36,610 --> 00:05:38,240
Serve me some more soup.

51
00:05:38,480 --> 00:05:39,340
Okay.

52
00:05:59,460 --> 00:06:02,050
(Random Chat)

53
00:06:05,780 --> 00:06:06,740
Go back.

54
00:06:19,600 --> 00:06:22,320
If my mom asks you
to drink in the future, just decline.

55
00:06:22,320 --> 00:06:24,030
Don't you dislike the smell?

56
00:06:26,150 --> 00:06:27,680
You came to get this, right?

57
00:06:28,270 --> 00:06:30,230
What future do we have?

58
00:06:36,180 --> 00:06:38,690
"When you want to be honest"

59
00:06:38,950 --> 00:06:41,430
and "When you want to confide in someone"—

60
00:06:41,580 --> 00:06:43,180
which of these two is better?

61
00:06:44,480 --> 00:06:46,060
"When you want to be honest."

62
00:06:46,060 --> 00:06:47,230
Right?

63
00:06:49,110 --> 00:06:51,110
The advertisers just have no taste.

64
00:06:51,280 --> 00:06:53,290
I've told them so many times
that this one is better.

65
00:06:53,290 --> 00:06:54,270
Did you call a designated driver?
Yeah.

66
00:06:55,630 --> 00:06:56,710
I just did.

67
00:06:57,220 --> 00:06:59,630
How long do you plan
to hide it from your mom?

68
00:07:00,590 --> 00:07:02,580
Since you're being so obvious about it,

69
00:07:02,580 --> 00:07:04,440
you might as well tell her sooner.

70
00:07:04,440 --> 00:07:06,050
Don't do it when I'm around.

71
00:07:07,620 --> 00:07:09,730
Didn't you take off your ring?

72
00:07:15,140 --> 00:07:16,410
Are you a teacher?

73
00:07:16,530 --> 00:07:17,710
Not yet.

74
00:07:18,880 --> 00:07:19,060
(Lee Hyunjae)

75
00:07:19,060 --> 00:07:20,390
You're a senior, right?
(Lee Hyunjae)

76
00:07:25,700 --> 00:07:27,370
I probably left it
when I went for the interview.

77
00:07:27,370 --> 00:07:28,970
Did you decide to work there?

78
00:07:29,550 --> 00:07:30,550
When do you start?

79
00:07:30,600 --> 00:07:31,460
Tomorrow.

80
00:07:32,290 --> 00:07:33,430
Which school?

81
00:07:34,900 --> 00:07:36,350
Nakwon High School.

82
00:07:42,130 --> 00:07:46,409
Did they ask you... to go there?

83
00:07:52,950 --> 00:07:55,210
My driver probably can't find their way.

84
00:07:55,390 --> 00:07:56,250
I'm leaving.

85
00:07:56,400 --> 00:07:57,200
Jiyoung.

86
00:08:04,300 --> 00:08:06,230
Stay the night and leave tomorrow.

87
00:08:09,630 --> 00:08:12,090
Wouldn't you be uncomfortable
with me here?

88
00:08:12,120 --> 00:08:13,420
Just have a good sleep.

89
00:08:13,970 --> 00:08:14,990
Go back.

90
00:08:16,600 --> 00:08:17,800
Hello, driver.

91
00:08:19,050 --> 00:08:21,650
I'm at the entrance of Building 303.

92
00:08:21,920 --> 00:08:23,160
I'll come to you.

93
00:08:29,730 --> 00:08:34,690
(Create a nickname)

94
00:08:44,320 --> 00:08:49,870
(Regret)

95
00:08:49,990 --> 00:08:53,200
(Nickname created)
(Nice to meet you! Regret, would you like to start a new chat?)

96
00:08:53,550 --> 00:08:54,300
(Yes)

97
00:09:05,420 --> 00:09:06,760
(Sunflower: Why is your nickname Regret?)

98
00:09:06,760 --> 00:09:08,640
Why is your nickname Regret?
(Sunflower: Why is your nickname Regret?)

99
00:09:14,510 --> 00:09:15,670
Well...

100
00:09:18,230 --> 00:09:20,780
I couldn't think of any other words.

101
00:09:22,730 --> 00:09:25,100
The first semester
of senior year is almost over

102
00:09:25,100 --> 00:09:26,450
but we have a new contract staff.

103
00:09:26,450 --> 00:09:28,720
How long will he take
to get the hang of it?

104
00:09:28,840 --> 00:09:30,540
And he's a fixed-term contract teacher.

105
00:09:30,540 --> 00:09:32,970
By the way, is Ms. Kim Haesook very sick?

106
00:09:33,170 --> 00:09:34,770
She's a senior homeroom teacher.

107
00:09:34,770 --> 00:09:36,280
I don't know either.

108
00:09:43,240 --> 00:09:45,270
I don't know how this sounds.

109
00:09:45,620 --> 00:09:50,200
This is Mr. Jang Kiwoo,
who is substituting for Ms. Kim Haesook.

110
00:09:55,010 --> 00:09:56,720
Nice to meet you.

111
00:10:05,500 --> 00:10:06,850
I feel regret for my situation.

112
00:10:06,850 --> 00:10:06,860
(Jang Kiwoo)
I feel regret for my situation.

113
00:10:06,860 --> 00:10:09,600
(Jang Kiwoo)

114
00:10:14,280 --> 00:10:17,080
Please take good care of me
for the remaining time.

115
00:10:18,250 --> 00:10:19,850
I'm going to start roll call.

116
00:10:20,640 --> 00:10:21,370
Shin Jaehak.
Here.

117
00:10:22,550 --> 00:10:23,150
Lee Jiyun.
Here.

118
00:10:24,100 --> 00:10:25,020
Lee Hyunjae.

119
00:10:29,430 --> 00:10:30,520
Lee Hyunjae?

120
00:10:37,610 --> 00:10:39,540
Can anyone contact Hyunjae?

121
00:10:44,380 --> 00:10:45,180
Next.
Joo Youngji.

122
00:10:46,030 --> 00:10:46,710
Here.

123
00:10:53,780 --> 00:10:55,440
If you call with your cell phone,
they might answer—

124
00:10:55,440 --> 00:10:57,640
though I don't know who you're calling.

125
00:10:59,890 --> 00:11:02,350
No one answers
a landline number these days.

126
00:11:02,440 --> 00:11:05,120
Communication has all been
moved over to KakaoTalk.

127
00:11:05,120 --> 00:11:07,900
Ah, that's the college application form.

128
00:11:08,030 --> 00:11:10,290
A student in our class
took the seniors' by mistake.

129
00:11:10,290 --> 00:11:11,660
Ah, okay.

130
00:11:18,770 --> 00:11:20,330
(Nakwon High School
College Application Form)

131
00:11:20,630 --> 00:11:28,910
(Nakwon High School College Application Form)
(Lee Hyunjae)

132
00:11:31,770 --> 00:11:32,700
Mr. Choi.

133
00:11:33,850 --> 00:11:35,980
If the parents'
contact information section is blank,

134
00:11:35,980 --> 00:11:37,440
How should I handle it?

135
00:11:37,570 --> 00:11:38,990
It's my first time seeing this.

136
00:11:38,990 --> 00:11:40,390
It's Lee Hyunjae, right?

137
00:11:43,200 --> 00:11:45,340
You were calling Hyunjae just now?

138
00:11:45,780 --> 00:11:48,150
We don't need to worry about
his college application.

139
00:11:48,150 --> 00:11:49,550
He'll probably go study abroad.

140
00:11:49,550 --> 00:11:51,150
His background is so strong.

141
00:11:51,820 --> 00:11:52,800
Background?

142
00:11:53,020 --> 00:11:54,040
Yeah.

143
00:11:54,200 --> 00:11:55,570
The chairman's son.

144
00:11:57,850 --> 00:12:00,910
You seem to be past the years
of caring for students.

145
00:12:01,490 --> 00:12:02,730
It's not like that.

146
00:12:03,340 --> 00:12:06,600
Then are you trying to score some points
with the chairman?

147
00:12:08,610 --> 00:12:09,960
Even if he leaves early
without saying a word,

148
00:12:09,960 --> 00:12:12,330
just treat it as he came to school.

149
00:12:12,610 --> 00:12:14,480
Maybe his family background is too strong.

150
00:12:14,480 --> 00:12:17,010
They don't allow any flaws on their child.

151
00:12:23,370 --> 00:12:25,170
Time is passing so slowly today.

152
00:12:25,190 --> 00:12:26,340
We should go eat lunch, right?

153
00:12:26,340 --> 00:12:27,580
Okay, let's go.

154
00:12:28,470 --> 00:12:32,330
Ah. Do you want to eat lunch with us?

155
00:12:34,230 --> 00:12:35,780
I'm good.

156
00:12:36,810 --> 00:12:38,580
I have plans.

157
00:12:38,910 --> 00:12:39,900
You're busy.

158
00:12:40,150 --> 00:12:40,960
Let's go.
Let's go.

159
00:12:50,960 --> 00:12:52,580
How regretful indeed—

160
00:12:52,580 --> 00:12:52,710
(How regretful indeed—
that no one is having lunch with you.)
How regretful indeed—
(How regretful indeed—
that no one is having lunch with you.)

161
00:12:53,320 --> 00:12:55,450
that no one is having lunch with you.
(How regretful indeed—
that no one is having lunch with you.)

162
00:13:50,000 --> 00:13:53,710
(Lee Hyunjae)

163
00:13:56,020 --> 00:13:58,080
I always run into you in weird places.

164
00:13:59,790 --> 00:14:01,140
Are you a teacher now?

165
00:14:01,490 --> 00:14:02,360
Yeah,

166
00:14:03,630 --> 00:14:04,960
your homeroom teacher.

167
00:14:12,650 --> 00:14:15,640
You didn't go
to the nurse's office last time, did you?

168
00:14:15,640 --> 00:14:16,640
I did.

169
00:14:19,590 --> 00:14:22,300
Actually, I didn't need
to go to the nurse's office.

170
00:14:22,300 --> 00:14:23,560
It's boring, isn't it?

171
00:14:23,900 --> 00:14:25,530
Going to school at your age.

172
00:14:26,140 --> 00:14:28,140
You skip classes whenever you want.

173
00:14:28,430 --> 00:14:29,600
It's not like that.

174
00:14:30,220 --> 00:14:31,290
Then what is it?

175
00:14:33,170 --> 00:14:35,010
You don't have to worry about me.

176
00:14:36,450 --> 00:14:37,520
Why?

177
00:14:38,600 --> 00:14:40,600
Because you're the chairman's son?

178
00:14:45,610 --> 00:14:46,550
Yes.

179
00:14:48,590 --> 00:14:51,790
I'll take care of myself.
You don't have to worry about me.

180
00:14:51,880 --> 00:14:53,040
Then...

181
00:14:54,860 --> 00:14:56,780
don't make me worry.

182
00:14:58,010 --> 00:14:59,780
I mean, take care of yourself,

183
00:15:00,010 --> 00:15:01,450
just like you said.

184
00:15:53,300 --> 00:15:54,190
Bro.

185
00:15:57,040 --> 00:15:58,160
It's your turn

186
00:15:58,920 --> 00:16:00,450
to take graduation photos.

187
00:16:02,280 --> 00:16:03,750
I'm not going to take one.

188
00:16:04,180 --> 00:16:05,280
It's compulsory.

189
00:16:10,570 --> 00:16:12,570
You didn't see anyone else, did you?

190
00:16:12,910 --> 00:16:14,140
Like Kim Jungha.

191
00:16:16,800 --> 00:16:17,840
Who's that?

192
00:16:18,010 --> 00:16:19,700
(Kim Jungha)

193
00:16:25,840 --> 00:16:27,400
Did Youngmoon send you?

194
00:16:28,170 --> 00:16:30,240
Where did he buy that drug?

195
00:16:30,520 --> 00:16:32,080
Can you tell me?

196
00:16:32,990 --> 00:16:34,520
How would I know?

197
00:16:35,090 --> 00:16:36,050
Just once.

198
00:16:38,490 --> 00:16:40,130
Just tell me the name.

199
00:16:40,840 --> 00:16:42,700
I'll buy it myself.

200
00:16:54,940 --> 00:16:57,110
Wow, look at that fucking restrained look.

201
00:16:57,110 --> 00:16:59,260
No wonder they call him
an obedient vending machine.

202
00:16:59,260 --> 00:17:00,570
He passes the test.

203
00:17:00,640 --> 00:17:01,290
Passed.

204
00:17:01,430 --> 00:17:02,600
What passed? Jeez.

205
00:17:02,730 --> 00:17:04,880
You couldn't even speak a word
in front of Kim Jungha.

206
00:17:04,880 --> 00:17:07,480
That's why
I'm talking behind his back, idiot.

207
00:17:10,260 --> 00:17:12,579
After the test,
the actual game officially begins.

208
00:17:12,579 --> 00:17:14,369
I'm really going to tell Lee Hyunjae

209
00:17:14,369 --> 00:17:15,369
to help buy the drug.

210
00:17:15,369 --> 00:17:18,349
Hey, he seems to be done.

211
00:17:25,760 --> 00:17:26,660
Bro.

212
00:17:26,990 --> 00:17:29,890
Let's talk.

213
00:17:37,100 --> 00:17:39,300
Fentanyl, cocaine, and stuff like that

214
00:17:39,330 --> 00:17:41,330
are too boring. No one will buy them.

215
00:17:41,420 --> 00:17:43,020
As long as you can get them,

216
00:17:43,410 --> 00:17:45,200
we'll find a way to sell them.

217
00:17:45,310 --> 00:17:46,440
As usual.

218
00:17:47,380 --> 00:17:49,440
There's that top-tier stuff, right?

219
00:17:49,590 --> 00:17:51,980
You seem to know a pharmacist.

220
00:17:52,110 --> 00:17:54,240
Just get a prescription,
grind it into powder, and bring it here.

221
00:17:54,240 --> 00:17:55,550
You know the drill.

222
00:17:55,880 --> 00:17:57,070
Why should I?

223
00:17:59,710 --> 00:18:00,860
Come on,

224
00:18:01,030 --> 00:18:03,280
we're discussing this nicely with you.

225
00:18:05,610 --> 00:18:07,740
I'm speaking nicely too.

226
00:18:11,120 --> 00:18:12,460
Why should I do this?

227
00:18:12,700 --> 00:18:15,900
Even if we get caught,
we'll just be sent to juvenile hall.

228
00:18:16,230 --> 00:18:17,760
You'll have to go to prison.

229
00:18:20,270 --> 00:18:21,470
Are you threatening me?

230
00:18:21,470 --> 00:18:24,360
Oh, if you think this is a threat,
I can't help it.

231
00:18:27,880 --> 00:18:31,580
If you want to threaten someone,
go find the bastard who threatened you.

232
00:18:31,580 --> 00:18:32,770
Go ahead.

233
00:18:33,490 --> 00:18:36,090
I don't care if you report it
or call the police.

234
00:18:45,090 --> 00:18:48,550
If we take this kid down,
we can definitely catch a pharmacist.

235
00:18:52,880 --> 00:18:54,130
Hey, it's me.

236
00:18:55,360 --> 00:18:57,830
I've given you a lot of money before.

237
00:18:57,950 --> 00:18:59,300
Just do me a favor.

238
00:19:10,380 --> 00:19:11,320
Hey.

239
00:19:14,650 --> 00:19:15,710
What are you doing?

240
00:19:16,200 --> 00:19:17,180
Part-time job.

241
00:19:17,300 --> 00:19:18,290
Part-time job?

242
00:19:19,690 --> 00:19:22,140
Hey, I don't have training today.

243
00:19:22,800 --> 00:19:24,100
Can I go to your place?

244
00:19:26,760 --> 00:19:28,420
Don't say things like that at school.

245
00:19:28,420 --> 00:19:29,420
What kind of part-time job are you doing?

246
00:19:29,420 --> 00:19:30,540
A darn good one.

247
00:19:31,330 --> 00:19:32,190
Hey.

248
00:19:33,070 --> 00:19:35,410
I see you're hanging out with Choi Youngmin.
Are you stealing things now?

249
00:19:35,410 --> 00:19:36,730
It's not like that.

250
00:19:37,810 --> 00:19:39,540
Just pretend you don't know.

251
00:19:39,740 --> 00:19:42,000
I already know. How can I pretend I don't?

252
00:19:43,140 --> 00:19:45,070
Just like how you usually treat me.

253
00:19:52,660 --> 00:19:53,720
Someone's coming.

254
00:19:59,070 --> 00:20:00,100
See?

255
00:20:01,780 --> 00:20:03,140
You're good at it.

256
00:20:04,350 --> 00:20:06,750
Pretending not to know
when you clearly do.

257
00:20:13,600 --> 00:20:15,060
I'll go over when I'm done.

258
00:20:26,190 --> 00:20:27,400
Hey, call my phone.

259
00:20:27,590 --> 00:20:28,420
Okay.

260
00:20:34,000 --> 00:20:36,260
I think I hear something from somewhere.

261
00:20:45,200 --> 00:20:47,300
Bro, can I take a look?

262
00:20:48,240 --> 00:20:50,270
I lost my phone.

263
00:20:50,440 --> 00:20:52,500
I heard a vibration coming from here.

264
00:20:54,900 --> 00:20:57,140
I heard you opened
the sports equipment room for him.

265
00:20:57,140 --> 00:20:59,160
Are you talking about Hyunjae?

266
00:21:01,300 --> 00:21:03,120
Yes, him.

267
00:21:04,110 --> 00:21:08,270
I mean, I'm keeping an eye on Hyunjae,

268
00:21:08,410 --> 00:21:10,240
so you don't need to worry.

269
00:21:11,910 --> 00:21:15,310
So... you knew he was
locked in the equipment room?

270
00:21:17,260 --> 00:21:18,920
He wasn't locked in.

271
00:21:19,960 --> 00:21:23,270
He just needed some time.

272
00:21:23,590 --> 00:21:27,770
You know those "thinking chairs"
that help people calm down and think?

273
00:21:28,990 --> 00:21:31,230
Just think of it as him sitting on
a thinking chair for a while.

274
00:21:31,230 --> 00:21:32,960
Does that make you feel better?

275
00:21:35,780 --> 00:21:38,070
Mr. Jang,
you might want to go take a look.

276
00:21:39,480 --> 00:21:42,270
I told you
there's a vibration coming from your bag.

277
00:21:42,270 --> 00:21:43,960
I just want to take a look.

278
00:21:44,100 --> 00:21:45,960
Are you trying to hide something?

279
00:21:47,070 --> 00:21:48,120
This is so weird.

280
00:21:48,250 --> 00:21:51,110
Everyone else let me see theirs.
Why won't you?

281
00:21:51,350 --> 00:21:53,520
Do you want me to open my bag for you?

282
00:21:53,680 --> 00:21:55,210
You guys open your bags too.

283
00:22:07,420 --> 00:22:08,540
It's your turn.

284
00:22:24,790 --> 00:22:26,910
It is you.

285
00:22:49,870 --> 00:22:52,710
Is this what you meant
by not making me worry

286
00:22:52,860 --> 00:22:54,460
and taking care of yourself?

287
00:22:59,950 --> 00:23:02,260
As long as you don't interfere, sir.

288
00:23:07,850 --> 00:23:09,060
Let's start class.

289
00:23:10,920 --> 00:23:14,180
Class starts in 5 minutes.
Everyone, go back to your seats.

290
00:23:28,260 --> 00:23:33,640
(Boy, with Caution)

291
00:23:34,080 --> 00:23:35,450
What? Stealing a phone?

292
00:23:35,700 --> 00:23:37,550
Didn't I tell you to behave
no matter what it takes you?

293
00:23:37,550 --> 00:23:38,410
Is it that hard?

294
00:23:38,410 --> 00:23:41,210
It's better to make him
reconcile with Youngmoon.

295
00:23:41,220 --> 00:23:42,250
Don't worry about anything.

296
00:23:42,250 --> 00:23:43,220
Lee Hyunjae.

297
00:23:43,360 --> 00:23:46,520
Just make sure his face is a bloody mess.

298
00:23:46,730 --> 00:23:48,230
I stole that phone.

299
00:23:48,550 --> 00:23:50,410
I just need to pay him back, right?

300
00:23:50,480 --> 00:23:52,370
Is this what the chairman asked for?

301
00:23:52,370 --> 00:23:54,610
Have you always been like this?

302
00:23:54,920 --> 00:23:58,200
I'm just curious
if you treat all students like this.

303
00:23:58,460 --> 00:24:00,230
Consider it special treatment.

304
00:24:00,230 --> 00:24:02,100
Yes, things like this happen.

305
00:24:02,380 --> 00:24:04,180
Sometimes I want to run away too.

306
00:24:04,220 --> 00:24:05,890
-It's getting late today—
-Mr. Jang.
